<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $48.7 mln Oct 23.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $48.7 mln Oct 23.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $48.7 million deficit on October 23 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 23</p>
<p>Exports: $164.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $235.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $436.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $414.5 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $48.7 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.788 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.952 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.939 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.064 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.711 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
